Q2: producer/consumer using counting semaphores and a lock

Build from lab2/ with the provided toolchain environment:
  mainframer.sh "make -C os && make -C apps/q2"
Alternatively, copy lab2 to /tmp and run those make commands there.
Build the OS first to provide the user libraries. No OS changes are needed.

Run from lab2/ after building:
  make -C apps/q2 run PAIRS=3
Or from lab2/bin/:
  dlxsim -x os.dlx.obj -a -u makeprocs.dlx.obj 3
The run target does not build executables. Q1, Q2, and the example share
output filenames in bin/. Clean and rebuild the desired application when
switching questions, so the simulator uses the correct executables.

Files:
  include/buffer.h        Shared circular buffer and synchronization handles.
  makeprocs/makeprocs.c   Initialize shared memory and start N pairs.
  producer/producer.c     Insert 0123456789 using empty-slot permits.
  consumer/consumer.c     Remove 0123456789 using full-slot permits.

The array has 32 entries; 31 are usable, retaining Q1's unused-slot
convention. s_emptyslots starts at 31 and s_fullslots starts at zero.
Producers wait for an empty slot before acquiring the lock, insert a
character, release the lock, and signal a full slot. Consumers wait for
a full slot before acquiring the lock. Neither process checks head/tail
for an empty or full condition; the semaphores manage availability.

A consumer removes only the front character, and only if it is its next
expected digit. On a mismatch it releases the lock, returns the full-slot
permit, and retries. On successful removal it signals an empty slot.
Thus empty/full waits block, while wrong-digit waits still retry. The
lock protects buffer access and operation prints. Children do not hold
the lock while waiting on a slot semaphore.

Completion follows the supplied example: the parent creates a semaphore
with count 1 - 2*N, waits once, and each child signals once after its last
operation. Inputs are restricted to 1..15 pairs because DLXOS has 32
process slots. Larger runs may need extra simulator memory, for example:
  dlxsim -m 0x1000000 -x os.dlx.obj -a -u makeprocs.dlx.obj 8
API failures print an error and exit; completion assumes children succeed.
process_create returns void, so it cannot be checked for a return status.

Before submission, clean all built applications and the OS. For Q2:
  make -C apps/q2 clean
  make -C os clean
Preserve the supplied lib/share_memory.o.

References:
  ECE 695 Fall 2026 Laboratory #2 handout supplied by the user.
  apps/q1, supplied apps/example, apps/Makerules, include/lab2-api.h,
  include/misc.h, and os/synch.c.
  Implementation assistance: OpenAI Codex in this workspace.
No external web sources were used.

Validation:
Built OS and Q2 in a temporary /tmp copy. Runs with 1, 3, and 4 pairs
used default simulator memory; 8 pairs used -m 0x1000000. Checked each
process's 0123456789 sequence, FIFO removals, buffer capacity, 10*N
insertion/removal counts, and graceful termination. Inputs 0, 16, abc,
and -1 were rejected. Test artifacts remain outside the source tree.
